<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ accommodation occupancy up in January - SNZ.</title>
<headline>NZ accommodation occupancy up in January - SNZ.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Accommodation occupancy increased in January, up to 42.6 percent, Statistics New Zealand said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>It said motels had the highest occupancy rate of 63.4 percent, up 10.9 percent from 52.5 percent in December. Caravan parks/campgrounds recorded the largest increase in occupancy of 11.5 percentage points to 29.1 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Excluding caravan parks/campgrounds, the national occupancy rate was 55.6 percent. This is up from 50.2 perent recorded in December,&quot; SNZ said.  </p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
